    "title": "Critique Codeweb user-centred value and paid-service strategy",
    "description": "The user asks how Codeweb can become indispensable and a clear purchase, with an extremely user-centred strategy grounded in the completed audit and public research. Root has written a candidate strategy at $LOCAL_HOME/Repositories/codeweb/reports/user-centric-value-strategy/STRATEGY.md. Independently critique that exact draft under the review-the-work skill; you are a different author/critic. Read the founder brief, charter boundary and reports/user-pain-research-2026-09-27/{README.md,OPPORTUNITY-DECISIONS.md,CONTRADICTIONS.md,REVIEW.md} as needed.\n\nYour task is a bounded critical review, not another collection swarm, implementation, outreach, pricing change, or charter change. Do not write a new strategy and approve your own version. Return PASS as a falsifiable proposal or REVISE with specific material corrections. Challenge whether it is sufficiently concrete and user-centred, whether every pain actually fits Codeweb capabilities, whether the conditional workflow would add burdens, whether hosting/cross-repo value exceeds ordinary CI, and whether any demand/ROI/retention claim is smuggled in. Verify the hypothetical price calculation is explicitly hypothetical. Name the weakest load-bearing assumption even on PASS. No new agents/services; preserve active homepage COD-67/COD-68. Use available existing-role capacity without interrupting delivery. One corrective attempt if required.\n\nSave a concise REVIEW.md in the management workspace under reports/user-centric-value-strategy and attach or link it in this issue. Record exact draft SHA-256, evidence checked, verdict, important limitations and actionable edits. Root will mirror the review into the requested repo. No new user decision is required for this critique. This task does not authorize running participant comparisons, recruitment sends, a paid pilot, or publication.",
